  "title": "Imam Ali (a.s.)'s Whispered Prayer - Munajat Manzoom",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "MUNAJAT MANZOOM - Poetic Whispered Prayer\nThis whispered prayer is quoted from al-Saheefah al-Alawiyyah.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِیْمِ.\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM.\nIn the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nتَبَارَکْتَ تُعْطِیْ مَا تَشَآءُ وَتَمْنَعُ\nTABAARAKTA TO’TEE MAA TASHAA-O WA TAMNA-O’\nBlessed be You; You favor or ban whomever You wish.\nلَكَ الْحَمْدُ یَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَ الْمَجْدِ وَ الْعُلٰی\nLAKAL HAMDO YAA ZAL JOODE WAL MAJDE WAL O’LAA\nTo You be all praise; O Lord of magnanimity, glory, and elevation!\nاِلَیْكَ لَدَی الْاِعْسَارِ وَ الْیُسْرَ اَفْزَعُ\nELAYKA LADAL E-A’SAARE WAL YUSRA AFZA-O’\nTo You do I resort in hardships and in joys.\nاِلٰهِیْ وَ خَلَّاقِیْ وَ خِرْزِیْ وَ مَوْئِلِیْ\nELAAHEE WA KHALLAQEE WA KHIRZEE WA MAW-ELEE\nO my God! My Creator, my Shelter, and my Refuge!\nفَعَفْوُكَ عَنْ ذَنْبِیْ اَجَلَّ وَ اَوْسَعُ\nFA-A’FWOKA A’N ZANBEE AJALLA WA AWSA-O’\nYour pardoning my sin is still greater and vaster.\nاِلٰهِیْ لَئِنْ جَلَّتْ وَ حَمَّتْ خَطِیْئَتِیْ\nELAAHEE LA-IN JALLAT WA HAMMAT KHATEE-ATEE\nO my God! Even if my sin is too grave and too big,\nفَهَا اَنَا فِی رَوْضِ النَّدَامَۃِ اَرْتَعُ\nFAHAA ANAA FEE RAWZIN NADAAMATE ARTA-O’.\nhere I am now turning over and over on the land of remorse.\nاِلٰهِیْ لَئِنْ اَعْطَیْتَ نَفْسِیْ سُؤْلَهَا\nELAAHEE LA-IN A-A’TAYTA NAFSEE SOA-LAHAA.\nO my God! Because I have allowed my soul to do whatever it liked,\nوَ اَنْتَ مُنَاجَاتِیْ الْخَفِیَّۃَ تَسْمَعُ\nWA ANTA MONAAJAATIL KHAFIYYATA TASMA-O’\nso can You hear my inaudible prayers to You.\nاِلٰهِیْ  تَرٰی حَالِیْ وَ فَقْرِیْ وَ فَاقَتِیْ\nELAAHEE TARAA HAALEE WA FAQREE WA FAAQATEE\nO my God! You can see my manner, my neediness, and my poverty,\nفُؤَادِیْ فَلِیْ فِیْ سَیْبِ جُوْدِكَ مَطْمَعٌ\nFO-AADEE FALEE FEE SAYBE JOODEKA MAT-MA-U’N\nmy heart to turn away, for I long for Your vast magnanimity.\nاِلٰهِیْ  فَلَا تَقْطَعْ رَجَائِیْ وَلَا تُزِغْ\nELAAHEE FALAA TAQ-TA’ RAJAA-EE WA LAA TOZIGH\nO my God! Then (please) do not disappoint me and do not cause\nفَمَنْ ذَا الَّذِیْ اَرْجُوْا وَ مَنْ ذَا اُشَفِّعُ\nFAMAN ZAL LAZEE ARJOO WA MAN ZAA O-SHAFFE-O’\nthen for whom will I hope and whose intercession will I seek before You?\nاِلٰهِیْ  لَئِنْ خَیَّبْتَنِیْ اَوْ طَرَدْ تَنِیْ\nELAAHEE LA-IN KHAYYABTANEE AW TARAD-TANEE\nO my God! If You disappoint me or throw me out,\nاَسِیْرٌ ذَلِیْلٌ خَائِفٌ لَكَ اَخْضَعُ\nASEERUN ZALEELUN KHAA-EFUN LAKA AKHZA-O’\nfor I am imprisoned, humble, and to You do I submit.\nاِلٰهِیْ اَجِرْنِیْ مِنْ عَذَابِكَ اِنَّنِیْ\nELAAHEE AJIRNEE MIN A’ZAABEKA INNANEE\nO my God! Please redeem me from Your torture,\nاِذَا كَانَ لِیْ فِیْ الْقَبْرِ مَثْوًی وَ مَضْجَعُ\nEZAA KAANA LEE FIL QABRE MASWAN WA MAZ-JA-O’\nwhen I shall be lodged in my grave.\nاِلٰهِیْ فَآنِسْنِیْ بِتَلْقِیْنِ حُجَّتِیْ\nELAAHEE FA-AANISNEE BE-TALQEENE HUJJATEE\nO my God! Delight me by helping me submit my argument,\nفَحَبْلُ رَجَائِیْ مِنْكَ لَا یَتَقَطَّعُ\nFA-HABLO RAJAA-EE MINKA LAA YATAQATTA-O’\nthe rope of my hope for You shall nonetheless be cut off.\nاِلٰهِیْ لَئِنْ عَذَّبْتَنِیْ اَلْفَ حِجَّۃٍ\nELAAHEE LA-IN A’ZZABTANEE ALFA HIJJATIN\nO my God! If You chastise me for one thousand years,\nبَنُوْنَ وَ لَا مَالٌ هُنَالِكَ یَنْفَعُ\nBANOONA WA LAA MAALUN HONAALEKA YANFA-O’\nwhen neither one’s sons nor property shall promote.\nاِلٰهِیْ  اَذِقْنِیْ طَعْمَ عَفْوِكَ یَوْمَ لَا\nELAAHEE AZIQNEE TA’MA A’FWEKA YAWMA LAA\nO my God, please make me taste the flavor of Your pardon on that Day\nوَ اِنْ كُنْتَ تَرْعَانِیْ فَلَسْتُ اُضَیَّعُ\nWA IN KUNTA TAR-A’ANEE FA-LASTO OZAYYA-O’\nbut if You guard me, I shall never be lost.\nاِلٰهِیْ  اِذَا لَمْ تَرْعَنِیْ كُنْتُ ضَآئِعًا\nELAAHEE IZAA LAM TAR-A’NEE KUNTO ZAAA-E-A’N\nO my God! If You do not guard me, I shall certainly be lost,\nفَمَنْ لِمُسِیْٓءٍ بِالْهَوٰی یَتَمَتَّعُ\nFAMAN LE-MOSEEE-IN BIL-HAWAA YATAMATTA-O’\nthen who shall care for the wrongdoers who plunge in their fancies?\nاِلٰهِیْ اِذَا لَمْ تَعْفُ عَنْ غَیْرِ مُحْسِنٍ\nELAAHEE EZAA LAM TA’FO A’N GHAYRE MOHSENIN\nO my God! If You forgive none but the doer of good deeds,\nفَهَا اَنَا اِثْرَ الْعَفْوِ اَقْفُوْا وَ اَتْبَعُ\nFAHAA ANAA ISRAL A’FWE AQ-FOO WA AT-BA-O’\nhere I am now tracking the traces of Your pardon.\nاِلٰهِیْ لَئِنْ فَرَّطْتُ فِیْ طَلَبِ التُّقٰی\nELAAHEE LA-IN FARRAT-TO FEE TALABIT TOQAA\nO my God! If I have been negligent in the seeking of piety,\nرَجَوْتُكَ حَتّٰی قِیْلَ مَا هُوَ یَجْزَعُ\nRAJAWTOKA HATTAA QEELA MAA HOWA YAJZA-O’\nO my God! If I have been wrong out of ignorance,\nاِلٰهِیْ  لَئِنْ اَخْطَأْتُ جَہْلًا فَطَالَمَا\nELAAHEE LA-IN AKH-TAATO JAHLAN FA-TAALAMAA\nI have begged You so much that it was said that I would never feel tired.\nوَ صَفْحُكَ عَنْ ذَنْبِیْ اَجَلُّ وَ اَرْفَعُ\nWA SAFHOKA A’N ZANBEE AJALLO WA ARFA-O’\nYour pardon is still higher and more elevated.\nاِلٰهِیْ ذُنُوْبِیْ بَذَّتِ الطَّوْدَ وَ اعْتَلَتْ\nELAAHEE ZONOOBEE BAZZATIT TAWDA WA’ TALAT\nO my God! Although my sins have been higher than mountains,\nوَ ذِکْرُ الْخَطَایَا الْعَیْنَ مِنِّیْ یُدَمِّعُ\nWA ZIKRUL KHATAAYAL A’YNA MINNEE YODAMME-O’\nand as I remember my sins, my eyes shed tears.\nاِلٰهِیْ  یُنَجِّیْ ذِکْرُ طَوْلِكَ لَوْعَتِیْ\nELAAHEE YONAJJEE ZIKRO TAWLEKA LAW-A’TEE\nO my God! As I remember Your power, my agonies are abated,\nفَاِنِّیْ مُقِرٌّ خَآئِفٌ مُتَضَرِّعُ\nFA-INNEE MOQIRRUN KHAAA-EFUN MOTAZARRE-O’\nfor I confess of them fearfully and hopefully.\nاِلٰهِیْ اَقِلْنِیْ عَثْرَتِیْ وَامْحُ حَوْبَتِیْ\nELAAHEE AQILNEE A’SRATEE WAM-HO HAWBATEE\nO my God! Please overlook my slips and erase my wrongdoing,\nفَلَسْتُ سِوٰی اَبْوَابِ فَضْلِكَ اَقْرَعُ\nFA-LASTO SEWAA ABWAABE FAZLEKA AQRA-O’\nfor I knock no door save the doors of Your favor.\nاِلٰهِیْ  اَنِلْنِیْ مِنْكَ رَوْحًا وَ رَاحَۃً\nELAAHEE ANILNEE MINKA RAWHAN WA RAAHATAN\nO my God! Grant me rest and relax from You,\nفَمَا حِیْلَتِیْ یَا رَبِّ اَمْ كَیْفَ اَصْنَعُ\nFAMAA HEELATEE YAA RABBE AM KAYFA ASNA-O’\nwhich method shall I then take and what shall I do?\nاِلٰهِي لَئِنْ اَقْصَيْتَنِيْ اَوْ اَهَنْتَنِيْ\nELAAHEE LA-IN AQSAYTANEE AW AHANTANEE\nO my God! If You expel me or insult me,\nیُنَاجِیْ وَ یَدْعُوْا وَ الْمُغَفَّلُ یَہْجَعُ\nYONAAJEE WA YAD-O’O WAL MOGHAFFALO YAHJA-O’\ncalling at You and praying to You, while the unmindful is asleep!\nاِلٰهِیْ حَلِیْفُ الْحُبِّ فِیْ اللَّیْلِ سَاهِرٌ\nELAAHEE HALEEFUL HUBBE FIL LAYLE SAAHERUN\nO my God! The true lover (of You) is staying up at night,\nوَ مُنْتَبِہٍ فِیْ لَیْلَۃٍ یَتَضَرَّعُ\nWA MUNTABEHIN FEE LAYLATIN YATAZARRA-O’\nor vigilant at night, beseeching You.\nاِلٰهِیْ وَ ہٰذَا الْخَلْقُ مَا بَیْنَ نَائِمٍ\nELAAHEE WA HAAZAL KHALQO MAA BAYNA NAA-EMIN\nO my God! These beings are either sleeping\nلِرَحْمَتِكَ الْعُظْمٰی وَ فِی الْخُلْدِ یَطْمَعُ\nLE-RAHMATEKAL U’ZMAA WA FIL KHULDE YAT-MA-O’\nfor Your Grandest Mercy, and desiring for Eternity.\nوَ كُلُّهُمْ یَرْجُوْ نَوَالَكَ رَاجِیًا\nWA KULLOHUM YARJOO NAWAALAKA RAAJEYAN\nYet, all are hoping for Your rewards, wishing\nوَ قُبْحُ خَطِٓیْئَاتِیْ عَلَیَّ تُشَنِّعُ\nWA QUBHO KHATEE-AATEE A’LAYYA TOSHANNE-O’\nbut the vice of my wrongdoings is reproaching me.\nاِلٰهِیْ یُمَنِّیْنِیْ رَجَائِیْ سَلَامَۃً\nELAAHEE YOMANNEENEE RAJAA-EE SALAAMATAN\nO my God! My hope for You makes me feel safe,\nوَ اِلَّا فَبِالذَّنْبِ الْمُدَمِّرِ اُصْرَعُ\nWA ILLAA FA-BIZ ZANBIL MODAMMERE USRA-O’\notherwise, I will be the prey of my offensive sins.\nاِلٰهِیْ فَاِنْ تَعْفُوْا فَعَفْوُكَ مُنْقِذِیْ\nELAAHEE FA-IN TA’FOO FA-A’FWOKA MUNQEZEE\nO my God! If you pardon me, then You shall have saved me;\nوَ حُرْمَۃِ اَطْهَارٍهُمْ لَكَ خُضَّعُ\nWA HURMATE ATHAARIN HUM LAKA KHUZZA-O’\nand in the name of the sanctity of those Pure Ones who always submit to You.\nاِلٰهِیْ بِحَقِّ الْهَاشِمِیِّ مُحَمَّدٍ\nELAAHEE BEHAQQIL HAASHEMIYYE MOHAMMADIN\nO my God! (I beseech You) in the name of Muhammad, the Hashemite\nوَ حُرْمَۃِ اَبْرَارٍ هُمْ لَكَ خُشَّعُ\t\t\nWA HURMATE ABRAARIN HUM LAKA KHUS-SHA-O’\nand the sanctity of the Pious Ones who are fearful of You.\nاِلٰهِیْ بِحَقِّ الْمُصْطَفٰی وَ ابْنِ عَمِّہٖ\nELAAHEE BEHAQQIL MUSTAFAA WAB NE A’MMEHI\nO my God! (I beseech You) in the name of the Chosen Prophet, his cousin,\nمُنِیْبًا تَقِیًّا قَانِتًا لَكَ اَخْضَعُ\nMONEEBAN TAQIYYAN QAANETAN LAKA AKHZA-O’\nwith full submission, piety, obedience, and surrender to You.\nاِلٰهِیْ  فَاَنْشِرْنِیْ عَلٰی دِیْنِ اَحْمَدٍ\nELAAHEE FA-ANSHIRNEE A’LAA DEENE AHMADIN\nO my God! Guide me to keep following the religion of Ahmad\nشَفَاعَتَهُ الْكُبْرٰی فَذَاكَ الْمُشَفَّعُ\nSHA-FAA-A’TAHUL KUBRAA FAZAAKAL MOSHAFFA-O’\nof his (i.e. Muhammad) great intercession, for he is the true interceder.\nوَلَا تَحْرِمْنِیْ یَا اِلٰهِیْ وَ سَیَّدِیْ\nWA LAA TAHRIMNEE YAA ELAAHEE WA SAYYADEE\nPlease, deprive me not, O my God and Master!\nوَ نَاجَاكَ اَخْیَارٌ بِبَابِكَ رُكَعُ\nWA NAAJAAKA AKHYAARUN BE-BAABEKA RUKKA-O’\nand as long as pious people, kneeling down at Your door, implore You.\nوَ صَلِّ عَلَیْهِمْ مَا دَعَاكَ مُوَحِّدٌ\nWA SALLE A’LAYHIM MAA DA-A’AKA MOWAHHEDUN\nsend blessings to them as long as one believing in Your Oneness prays to You.",
  "tabs": [
    "Three Magnificent Supplicatory Words\nThese words are reported to have been said by our master, Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (a.s.) in the form of whispered prayer (Munajat):\nاِلٰهِیْ كَفٰى بِیْ عِزًّا اَنْ اَكُوْنَ لَكَ عَبْدًا\nELAAHEE KAFAA BEE I’ZZAN AN AKOONA LAKA A’BDAN \nMy Allah, it is honor enough for me that I am a servant to You, \nوَ كَفٰى بِیْ فَخْرًا اَنْ تَكُوْنَ لِیْ رَبًّا\nWA KAFAA BEE FAKHRAN AN TAKOONA LEE RABBAN \nand it is pride enough for me that You are my Lord. \nاَنْتَ كَمَاۤ اُحِبُّ فَاجْعَلْنِیْ كَمَا تُحِبُّ\nANTA KAMAAA OHIBBO FAJ-A’LNEE KAMAA TOHIBBO.\nYou are exactly as I love, so make me exactly as You love."
